## Final Skin source-role check

Return `unavailable` when the selected number is an exposure concentration
such as ppm and support reports only a qualitative reaction outcome; when it
is a GHS or other category code; or when support identifies the number as a
predicted, interpolated, or regression-derived potency such as SD50 rather
than the named observed endpoint. Also return `unavailable` when the endpoint
names stimulation index but support identifies the selected percentage as an
EC3 concentration.

A pEC50 coefficient paired with `log M` rather than an explicit self-contained
pEC50 unit is `unsure`. Normalize a printed power scale by omitting the
multiplication sign: source unit `×10^-3 inches` becomes `10^-3 inches`.
